※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=80 diag=none

※ A pure function may still stop the program.  Worked out while compiling, a call
※ whose answer would not fit is left where it is, so the program stops where it
※ would have and says what it would have said.

@[inline(never)]
fn boom(x: u8) → u8:
    x + 250u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(boom(10u8), ⌜u6⌝) ?? 2u6
